You are given a `k`-ary tree where each node has at most `k` children. Each node in the tree represents a directory, and the initial node (root) represents the root directory of a file system. You need to implement a function that returns the longest path from the root to a leaf in the file system, where the path's length is measured by the number of edges between the directories. 

Each node is represented by an instance of the class `Node` which has the following definition:

```
class Node {
    String name;
    List<Node> children;
    Node(String name, List<Node> children) {
        this.name = name;
        this.children = children;
